:: stage2-BFGRecap-vn-transcript-eng [nobr]
<p>Transcript:</p>
<p>A recap- sure thing. </p>

<p>So, there’s a little girl called Sophie, who meets the BFG - BFG stands for Big Friendly Giant. The BFG collects and delivers sweet dreams to children with a special dream-blower trumpet. </p>

<p>The BFG carries Sophie off to faraway Giant Country and there are other giants there. However, unlike the 9 other terrifying and enormous giants who eat humans, the BFG lives on Snozzcumbers. Remember the stain on the letter? </p>

<p>Sophie and the BFG become friends and the BFG takes Sophie to see Dream Country, the home of all the dreams! Here she learns about Dreams and they collect some, in the BFG’s net, and then put them into the BFG’s Dream Jars! </p>

<p>However, one night the human-eating giants are planning to go eat, so the BFG and Sophie hatch a brave plan to stop the human-eating giants by delivering a special dream to the Queen (yes the Queen!) that will help prove the existence of Giants and show her their horrible plan. When the Queen wakes up, Sophie is in her bedroom and The Queen realises her dream was actually true, and Sophie introduces the Queen to the BFG. </p>

<p>After talking with the BFG, The Queen agrees to help and, with the support of the army, the BFG and Sophie travel back to Giant Country and capture the man-eating giants with helicopters. The giants are taken away and the BFG is given a special title from the Queen - the ‘Royal Dream-Blower’. </p>

